# Concave and Convex Models

Models with diminishing or increasing returns. Concave models capture situations where each additional unit of input produces less output (diminishing returns). Convex models capture increasing returns where additional input produces progressively more output.

## Key Insight

Understanding whether a system is concave or convex changes strategy entirely. Concave systems favor diversification and caution; convex systems favor concentration and bold bets. This connects to [[bet-sizing]] and [[expected-value-ev]].

## Applications

- Learning curves (concave)
- Network effects (convex)
- Resource allocation
- Investment strategy

